The PNG files in this directory are the authoritative pixel-perfect goldens
for the html2slides pipeline.

THEY MAY ONLY BE WRITTEN BY THE HUMAN USER, and only via the SxS rating UI
(rating-server.ts) when the user explicitly clicks "Good" on a slide.

Claude / any script / any automated tool MUST NEVER:
  - Copy PNGs into this directory directly.
  - Run `check-goldens.ts --bless` (the flag is disabled and will error out).
  - Run `cp`, `mv`, or editor writes targeting `goldens/*.png`.
  - Commit regenerated thumbnails as goldens.

If a fix is complete, regen and diff against goldens. Then PRESENT the diff
to the user and let them rate in SxS. Blessing is not a Claude action.

Rationale: goldens are the human-approved truth. Letting the automated loop
"bless" its own output collapses the feedback signal — the system would
always report "no regressions" because it would always promote whatever it
produced.
